WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.186
Week 25: Future, Probability, and Forecasting. make forecasts state commitments express probability about the present

2
00:00:08.186 --> 00:00:20.791
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can make forecasts, state commitments, express probability about the present. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:20.791 --> 00:00:29.126
Language system. Simple future; irregular stems; future of probability; time clauses referring to future events.

4
00:00:29.126 --> 00:00:36.224
Sound and delivery. Future endings and sentence stress that distinguishes certainty from speculation.

5
00:00:36.224 --> 00:00:45.650
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:45.650 --> 00:01:14.383
Model language. La población urbana aumentará. — The urban population will increase. Seguiremos midiendo los resultados. — We will continue measuring the results. ¿Dónde estará Marta ahora? — Where could Marta be now? Cuando termine el estudio, publicaremos los datos. — When the study ends, we will publish the data. Dentro de cinco años habrá nuevas opciones. — Within five years there will be new options.

7
00:01:14.383 --> 00:01:24.302
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
